[% META title = 'Theme Configuration' %]
[% PageVersion = 'ThemeConfig.tt,v 0.01 2025/01/19 shanta Exp shanta ' %]
[% debug %]
[% IF c.session.debug_mode == 1 %]
    [% PageVersion %]
    [% "Debugging HostName: " _ HostName %]
    [%# INCLUDE 'debug.tt' %]
[% END %]

<div class="documentation-content">
    <h1>Theme Configuration</h1>

    <section class="overview">
        <div class="alert alert-warning">
            <strong>Updated Guidance</strong>: Canonical definitions live at <code>/static/config/theme_definitions.json</code>
        </div>
        <p>Theme system now reads from the canonical <code>theme_definitions.json</code> file in <code>static/config/</code>. All code paths should reference this single source of truth for themes and mappings.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="recent-enhancements">
        <h2>Storage &amp; Production (2026-08-17)</h2>
        <div class="enhancement-highlight">
            Theme state now lives in two paths <strong>inside</strong> <code>root/static</code> (<code>static/config/theme_definitions.json</code> and <code>static/css/themes/*.css</code>), backed by persistent volume overlays (<code>comserv2_theme_config</code>, <code>comserv2_theme_css</code>). The old read-only host bind (<code>./root/static:/opt/comserv/root/static:ro</code>) that caused the <code>Permission denied</code> / <code>No such file or directory</code> writes was removed. For the full admin guide, see <a href="[% c.uri_for('/Documentation/CssThemes') %]">/Documentation/CssThemes</a> (Storage &amp; Production + Roadmap sections).
        </div>
    </section>

    <section class="recent-enhancements">
        <h2>Resilience Note &mdash; Missing Config Directory</h2>
        <div class="enhancement-highlight">
            <strong>2026-08-12</strong>: All JSON writers (<code>set_site_theme</code>,
            <code>create_theme</code>, <code>save_theme</code>, <code>set_site_favicon</code>,
            <code>set_domain_favicon</code>) now call an internal
            <code>_ensure_parent_dir</code> guard that <code>mkdir -p</code>s
            <code>static/config/</code> before writing. Previously, <code>write_file</code>
            raised <code>ENOENT</code> when that directory was absent on a deployment
            (e.g. the production container), which surfaced as a repeated
            <code>set_site_theme</code> error on every MCoop page load. See
            <a href="/Documentation/changelog/2026-08-12-themeconfig-missing-dir-fix">ThemeConfig set_site_theme ENOENT Fix</a>.
        </div>
    </section>

    <section class="recent-enhancements">
        <h2>Recent Enhancements</h2>
        <div class="enhancement-highlight">
            <strong>Interactive Theme Editor</strong>: The theme system now includes a comprehensive interactive CSS editor with real-time preview capabilities. See the <a href="/Documentation/changelog/2025-01-19-css-theme-system-enhancements.tt">CSS Theme System Enhancements - January 2025</a> changelog for complete details on new features including:
        </div>
        <ul class="feature-list">
            <li>Interactive CSS editing interface</li>
            <li>Enhanced Theme Management Controller with CSC admin access controls</li>
            <li>New CSS file structure and Template Toolkit integration</li>
            <li>Advanced theme variable management</li>
        </ul>
    </section>

    <section class="related-documentation">
        <h2>Related Documentation</h2>
        <ul class="documentation-links">
            <li><a href="/static/css/README_THEME_SYSTEM.tt">Theme System Overview</a> - Technical documentation for the CSS theme system</li>
            <li><a href="/Documentation/admin/theme_mappings_handling.tt">Theme Mappings Handling</a> - Git operations and theme mapping management</li>
        </ul>
    </section>
</div>